---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What the quote form collects, who processes it and for how long."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy"
    intro="Short version: no tracking. The quote form sends what you enter to the shop by email, and your files to a private store."
  />
  <div class="container prose">
    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a fictional company. This website is a design and engineering demo by{' '}
      {site.demoBy}. It has no analytics, no cookies, no tracking pixels and no third-party scripts
      or fonts.
    </p>
    <h2>The quote form</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>What it collects:</strong> your name, company, work email and phone (optional), what
      you write about the part (description, quantities, material, process, tolerance, finishing,
      paperwork, date, notes) and the drawings you attach.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Why:</strong> only to answer that request: the details reach the shop by email, and
      you get a confirmation with your request number. Nothing is used for marketing, sold or shared
      beyond the services below.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Who processes it:</strong>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Resend</strong> delivers the two emails (to the shop and your confirmation).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the site and the form's server code. Your files go straight
        from your browser to a <strong>private Vercel Blob store</strong>: they have no public
        address. The shop's email contains signed links that stop working after 7 days; after that
        the files can be opened only by the site owner from the Vercel dashboard.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>How long:</strong> the emails stay in the mailboxes and the files in the store until
      the site owner deletes them; there is no automatic deletion. To have your request deleted,
      email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with your request number.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Abuse protection:</strong> to limit automated sending, the server counts requests per
      IP address in its memory for up to an hour. Its own logs record request numbers and error
      codes only, never names, addresses or file names.
    </p>
    {site.demo && (
      <p>
        <strong>On this demo:</strong> {site.name} is fictional, so requests and confirmations go to
        the developer's test inbox, not to a machine shop or to you, and nobody prepares a quote.
        Please do not send real or confidential drawings.
      </p>
    )}
    <h2>What the browser remembers</h2>
    <p>
      Two settings are saved in your browser's local storage so pages look the way you left them:
      whether you hid the demo notice, and whether you chose inches or millimeters. They never leave
      your device. Clear your site data to remove them.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      Like any website, the server that delivers these pages may keep standard access logs (IP
      address, time, page requested) for security and operations, under the host's own policy.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
